I was recently pondering the latest craze which puts the PYEC
high up on the list of things to wish for.  It seems that only
Neutral characters can do anything with it, but I wonder if it
should appear for any non-Tourist at all?

One thing I thought was cool about the Quest thing was that
each Class had it's own quest.  I thought it was real nice that
there was 'finally' a way that the game could still vary between
differing character classes beyond the first 10 levels of the game.

If anyone can get PYEC's, Hearts of Ahriman, Sceptres of Might,
doesn't that kind of diminish the Uniqueness of each item?
Could we possibly make all these artifacts off limits for wishes
(except for the Wizard mode, of course).

I also was led to wonder about wishing for the other Artifacts
in the game, many of which have implicit alignments.  I would think
that a Lawful God would never hand out Stormbringer, etc.

I was then led to consider the following proposal for granting
artifacts for wishes:

    demons     chaotic only
    djinni     neutral only
    thrones    lawful only (unless they are demon thrones)
    WOW        anything -- but your God will listen in
               bad thing for a Knight to wish for Stormbringer....


Now, if your Knight really wanted to get a Stormbringer, he'd have
to find himself a Helm of Opposite Alignment, and then start to
make some offers on a Chaotic altar... or some such.

Now there's an idea....

